WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
Most nerve cells never divide again.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.830
They keep the same DNA
for their whole life.

3
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.250
In cells with a nucleus, that
DNA stays inside the nucleus.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.290
But proteins are made on
ribosomes, out in the cytoplasm.

5
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.200
So how do the instructions in DNA reach
the place where proteins are made?

6
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:24.140
In this mission, you'll watch an enzyme
unwind part of a gene and read just one

7
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.930
of its two strands.

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.920
Then you'll write out
three matching sequences,

9
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:32.030
base by base, and spot what links them.

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.050
Your mission: find out how instructions
in DNA reach the place where proteins

11
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:37.720
are made.
